  "content": {
    "title": "As it happened: Michigan State women's hoops lose close game to Oklahoma",
    "text": "Updated March 22, 2026, 10:31 p.m. ETMichigan State women's basketball ended its season with a loss to the Oklahoma Sooners on Sunday, March 22.After knocking off No. 12 seed Colorado State to advance to the second round of the NCAA Tournament, the Spartans loss to Oklahoma on Sunday night, missing the Sweet 16 in Sacramento, California.The 5-seed Spartans loss to the Sooners in the second round of the NCAA Tournament at Lloyd Noble Center in Norman, Oklahoma, 77-71.The Sooners, meanwhile, knocked off No. 13 seed Idaho easily, 89-59, on Friday, March 21, to open the NCAA Tournament. They will be headed to the Sweet 16 for the second straight season to face either South Carolina or USC in Sacramento. Watch Michigan-N.C. State Women's March Madness on FuboThis is MSU's third consecutive season with an NCAA tournament appearance.Here's a recap of the game:Michigan State vs Oklahoma NCAA Tournament live game score updatesMSU's season ends to OUFinal: Michigan State 67, Oklahoma 74.The Spartans came into the game the smaller team and it hurt them tonight.Beers ended the game with 18 points and 14 rebounds over 29 minutes.MSU ends the season 23-9, their most wins since 2016.Freshman Chaves hits shot to put OU up sevenQ4, 2:46 Michigan State 67, Oklahoma 74.Chavez, who has climbed out of her first half shooting slump hit a critical three at the right time to put the Sooners up seven.She and Beers have a combined 36 points.OU hits crucial threeQ4, 6:30: Michigan State 58, Oklahoma 66.After both teams traded baskets to start the fourth quarter, OU is starting to look like No. 3 scoring offense in the nation.Verhulst hit a 24-foot three pointer on a Vann assist, prompting MSU timeout.MSU sticks around after physical quarterEnd of Q3: Michigan State 54, Oklahoma 57In a physical third quarter, both teams are starting to feel the weight of the game with a trip to the Sweet 16 on the line.Officials seem to be calling the game tighter as tension between OU and MSU have started to rise.After review, MSU's Brown was given a Flagrant 1 foul, resulting in a pair of knocked down free throws by Chavez.Michigan State ended the quarter on a 6-0 run.MSU lead vanishes to start halfQ3, 7:43: Michigan State 42, Oklahoma 45.Beers knocked down a 16 and 17-foot jumper to cap off an 8-0 run by Oklahoma and give them the lead against MSU.Michigan State has not yet scored in the third quarter.Nine lead changes for OU and MSU so far this gameHalftime: Michigan State 42, Oklahoma 37MSU so far tonight has slowed down Chavez, a former No. 1 overall recruit who is playing in her first NCAA tournament. She shot 3-11 to end the first half.Beers however, OU's second highest scorer has 11 points and five rebounds.MSU's Jones, who came off the bench after starting all season is leading all players with 16 points.Additionally, she is also guarding Chavez.This game so far has had nine lead changes, the most of any first half in March Madness this year.What feels like sloppy play is good defense from both teamsQ2, 4:10: Michigan State 29, Oklahoma 31.After two back-to-back buckets from the Oklahoma Sooners, Vanslooten was blocked by Beers and the energy felt like it was changing in Sacramento.MSU, although down, seems to have weathered the storm with Emma Shumate taking a key charge before shooting a 24-foot three pointer at the 5:34 mark.Beers also made a 16-foot jumper off a Chavez assist at the 4:51 mark to put the Sooners up two.MSU up early against OUEnd of Q1: Michigan State 21, Oklahoma 16.Shooting woes were the theme of the first quarter for MSU's last matchup against Colorado.This game, they are shooting significantly better, around 53% from the field, opposed to their 35% to end the first Friday night.Rashunda Jones is currently leading the Spartans in scoring with nine points. Vanslooten has also contributed four.Both Beers and Brook for OU have a combined 10 points.Vanslooten, Beers matchupBoth Vanslooten and Beers are the talk of the game as both bigs played one another in the 2022 McDonald's All-American game and four other times at previous schools.They both also played for Team USA in the 2025 FIBA Women's AmeriCup.A quick, competitive start for both OU and MSUQ1, 5:00: Michigan State 11, Oklahoma 10.Michigan State, who started a different lineup this game since their last timeout have seemed to match both OU's size and speed so far this game.At the 5:09 mark, Chavez received an outlet pass after a Verhulst steal and attempted to make a fast break layup before being blocked by MSU's VanSlooten,Michigan State starting fiveG Kennedy BlairG Jalyn BrownF Inés SoteloF Isaline AlexanderF Grace VanslootenOklahoma starting fiveG Aaliyah ChavezG Zya VannG Peyton VerhulstG Sahara WilliamsC Raegan BeersBoth teams have the ability to score in bunchesA high-scoring affair is expected for the matchup between the Spartans and the Sooners.OU averages 86.8 points per game while the Spartans average 82.5, ESPN analytics say.Michigan State basketball vs Oklahoma game timeDate: Sunday, March 22.Time: 8 p.m.Location: Norman, Oklahoma.Michigan State basketball vs Oklahoma TV channelTipoff: 8 p.m.Channel: ESPN.Streaming: Fubo (free trial).Radio: WJR-AM 760 (Detroit), WJIM-AM 1240 (Lansing).Michigan State's second round game against Oklahoma can be watched and streamed on Fubo, which carries ESPN channels.Watch Michigan-N.C. State Women's March Madness on FuboNCAA women's tournament Final Four locationDates: April 3, 5.Location: Mortgage Matchup Center, Phoenix.Jalen Williams is a trending reporter at the Detroit Free Press. Contact him at jawilliams1@freepress.com.",
